e, interval or box plot is given.\"},\n  \"S6_metrics\": {\"code\": \"B\", \"quote\": \"Fig 12. Confusion matrix in the test dataset, (a) CWRU dateset, (b) SBTP dateset.\", \"location\": \"p.15\", \"reason\": \"Test-set confusion matrices are shown (Fig 12). Tables 2 and 3 give per-class Precision, Recall and F1-Score, and Table 4 gives Accuracy and F1.\"},\n  \"S7_noise_protocol\": {\"code\": \"U\", \"quote\": \"Table 4. Performance comparison of different models in different SNR levels.\", \"location\": \"p.17\", \"reason\": \"Results are reported at SNR = -2, 0, 2 and 4 dB. The paper never says whether noise was added only to test data or to both training and test data, nor how the noise was generated.\"},\n  \"S8_traceability\": {\"code\": \"G\", \"quote\": \"Training process analysis: Fig 11 illustrates the evolution of loss and accuracy metrics during the training process.\", \"location\": \"p.14\", \"reason\": \"No code, weights or raw result files are released; the data availability statement only points to the public CWRU data. The only traceability material is the per-epoch loss and accuracy curves in Fig 11, coded as G. If the coding team counts only separately released log files, this should be 0.\"}\n}\n```",
